About

    This subdirectory contains a patch that exposes AGAMA's Fortran standard interface to Ramses, and couples it to my oagertz/dice patch.

    See ../agama/README for more information

Usage

    Compile Ramses patch with either of:

        - Makefile_3D_GNU_OLDMPI0_OAGERTZ_AGAMA_DICEPATCH
        - Makefile_3D_GNU_OLDMPI0_OAGERTZ_AGAMA_DICEPATCH_WH07

    In the NML, include the following block:

    ! file path is set by initfile (in INIT_PARAMS):
    &AGAMA_PARAMS
    agama_file = 'some_agama_potential.ini'
    agama_verbose = .false. ! (default: .true.)
    t_step = 0.0            ! controls the file read frequency (default: 1e10)
    /

    ALSO IMPORTANT: Requires gravity_type < 0

    &POISSON_PARAMS
    gravity_type=-1
    /

    Furthermore, MAY NEED TO ADJUST mass_sph in &REFINE_PARAMS.../ to match a fully responsive analogue.

    See Notes below.

Notes
    - 'agama_file' is either an INI file with [Potential] section, either specifing an analytic potential or with a potential approximation and derivatives (with its coefficients, etc.)
    - 'agama_verbose' provides output to stdout about when and which INI file is read
    - the file is read at every 't_step'; the default value of t_step = 1e10 means the file is only read at t = 0.


